WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
Wendy was awakened by Peter's crying.

2
00:00:03.641 --> 00:00:08.895
She wasn't very frightened to see the strange boy sitting on the nursery floor.

3
00:00:08.896 --> 00:00:11.773
Instead she was curious about him.

4
00:00:11.774 --> 00:00:14.827
She had almost expected him to be there.

5
00:00:14.828 --> 00:00:21.454
"Boy," she asked softly, "what is your name and why are you crying?"

6
00:00:21.455 --> 00:00:27.081
Forgetting his own troubles for the moment, Peter got up from the floor and bowed graciously.

7
00:00:27.082 --> 00:00:30.146
He knew how to act properly when he wanted to.

8
00:00:30.147 --> 00:00:36.479
"Let me introduce myself," he said. "I'm Peter Pan. What's your name?"

9
00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.812
"I'm Wendy Darling," replied Wendy. "Where do you come from?"

10
00:00:41.813 --> 00:00:48.450
"I live at the second star to the right, and then straight on till morning," Peter said.

11
00:00:48.451 --> 00:00:52.793
"What a funny address. Is that where you get mail?"

12
00:00:52.794 --> 00:00:55.223
"I don't get any mail."

13
00:00:55.224 --> 00:00:58.401
"But your mother must get mail."

14
00:00:58.402 --> 00:01:01.896
"I don't have a mother," said Peter.

15
00:01:01.897 --> 00:01:07.799
"I'm so sorry you don't have a mother," Wendy said sympathetically.

16
00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.456
"That's not why I'm upset," said Peter.

17
00:01:11.457 --> 00:01:16.026
"I'm upset because I can't get my shadow to stick back on me."

18
00:01:16.027 --> 00:01:20.129
"I can fix that," Wendy answered helpfully.

19
00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:24.526
She went to get the sewing kit and sewed the shadow onto Peter's feet.

20
00:01:24.527 --> 00:01:28.428
When she was done, his shadow was as good as new.

21
00:01:28.429 --> 00:01:37.995
Peter gave a howl of delight. "How clever I am!" he crowed, jumping about.

22
00:01:37.996 --> 00:01:42.363
He had already forgotten that it was Wendy who had solved his problem.

23
00:01:42.364 --> 00:01:46.059
Wendy reminded him of her part in his good fortune.

24
00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:52.189
So he replied, "Wendy, one girl is more useful than twenty boys."

25
00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:54.862
He didn't want to offend her.

26
00:01:54.863 --> 00:01:59.353
Touched by his sweet words, Wendy offered to give him a kiss.

27
00:01:59.354 --> 00:02:03.013
But Peter didn't understand what a kiss was.

28
00:02:03.014 --> 00:02:07.922
Suddenly becoming shy, Wendy handed him a thimble instead.

29
00:02:07.923 --> 00:02:12.046
"Now I will give you a kiss too," Peter said.

30
00:02:12.047 --> 00:02:18.253
Thinking a kiss was a present, he dropped a button in the shape of an acorn into her hand.

31
00:02:18.254 --> 00:02:21.174
Wendy put the button on a chain around her neck.

32
00:02:21.175 --> 00:02:25.451
"I promise to wear this forever," she said.

33
00:02:25.452 --> 00:02:27.996
Wendy asked Peter how old he was.

34
00:02:27.997 --> 00:02:31.507
"I'm still very young," said Peter.

35
00:02:31.508 --> 00:02:36.178
"I didn't want to ever grow up, so I ran away when I was born.

36
00:02:36.179 --> 00:02:39.108
I went to live with the fairies."

37
00:02:39.109 --> 00:02:44.010
Wendy wanted to know everything about fairies and asked many questions.

38
00:02:44.011 --> 00:02:52.332
Peter explained that when the first baby ever born laughed for the first time, its laugh broke into a thousand pieces.

39
00:02:52.333 --> 00:02:57.776
The pieces all went skipping around, and that was the beginning of fairies.

40
00:02:57.777 --> 00:03:04.874
He also said there should be one fairy for every boy and girl, but children grow old too soon.

41
00:03:04.875 --> 00:03:08.766
"And they stop believing in fairies," said Peter.

42
00:03:08.767 --> 00:03:14.672
"Each time a child says 'I don't believe in fairies,' a fairy dies."

43
00:03:14.673 --> 00:03:22.106
While he was speaking of fairies, Peter suddenly remembered Tinker Bell, who had been quiet all this time.

44
00:03:22.107 --> 00:03:26.746
When he called her name, a tinkling sound came from the chest of drawers.

45
00:03:26.747 --> 00:03:31.497
"What's that? It sounds like bells," said Wendy.

46
00:03:31.498 --> 00:03:34.319
"That's Tinker Bell, my fairy friend.

47
00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:41.606
I think I accidentally shut her in the drawer," Peter laughed.

48
00:03:41.607 --> 00:03:45.907
When he opened the drawer, Tinker Bell darted from place to place.

49
00:03:45.908 --> 00:03:51.025
She screamed angry words that only Peter could understand.

50
00:03:51.026 --> 00:03:55.834
"You shouldn't say such naughty things!" he responded.

51
00:03:55.835 --> 00:04:00.378
Wendy was totally delighted that there was a fairy in her nursery.

52
00:04:00.379 --> 00:04:07.075
When Tinker Bell finally stood still on the cuckoo clock, Wendy cried, "Oh she's so lovely!"

53
00:04:07.076 --> 00:04:10.516
Tinker Bell replied something in fairy language.

54
00:04:10.517 --> 00:04:13.693
Then she disappeared into the bathroom.

55
00:04:13.694 --> 00:04:17.176
"What is she saying, Peter?" Wendy asked.

56
00:04:17.177 --> 00:04:22.833
"Tink says you are an ugly girl," he replied, a bit too honestly.

57
00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:26.846
"You see, she is a common fairy and isn't very polite."

58
00:04:26.847 --> 00:04:30.385
Wendy continued to question Peter about himself.

59
00:04:30.386 --> 00:04:34.694
"If you don't live with your mother, who do you live with?"

60
00:04:34.695 --> 00:04:38.151
Peter told her that he lived with the Lost Boys.

61
00:04:38.152 --> 00:04:42.538
They were children who had fallen out of their strollers as infants.

62
00:04:42.539 --> 00:04:47.486
These boys had been taken to Neverland, where Peter was their captain.

63
00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:52.922
He continued, "Sadly, we are all boys, with no girls around.

64
00:04:52.923 --> 00:04:56.419
And sometimes we get very lonely.

65
00:04:56.420 --> 00:05:00.108
For instance, there is no one to tell us stories.

66
00:05:00.109 --> 00:05:04.740
That's why I sometimes come to your nursery and listen to your stories.

67
00:05:04.741 --> 00:05:11.402
The other night your mother was telling such a lovely story about the lady with the glass slippers."

68
00:05:11.403 --> 00:05:13.919
"Peter, that was Cinderella.

69
00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:19.937
And her prince found her and they lived happily ever after," Wendy explained.

70
00:05:19.938 --> 00:05:23.680
Peter was so excited that he rose and hurried to the window.

71
00:05:23.681 --> 00:05:26.667
"Where are you going?" Wendy cried.

72
00:05:26.668 --> 00:05:30.807
"To tell the other boys the end of that story."

73
00:05:30.808 --> 00:05:36.180
"Don't go, Peter," she pleaded. "I know so many other stories.

74
00:05:36.181 --> 00:05:40.274
Oh, the stories I could tell you and the Lost Boys!"

75
00:05:40.275 --> 00:05:49.449
When he heard this, Peter hurried back to her with a greedy look in his eyes.

